saveOutputs: false
cells:
  - kind: 1
    value: "# Demo – Just a sprain? (live)\n\nThe queries we run live, in the order of the talk: one for step 1, two each for steps 2–6 (slides 15–20) and the finale (slide 21). The SQL is copied unchanged from the notebooks 11a–11h. Run as the demo user (DOAG2026) from top to bottom.\n\n> Fictitious demo: no medical device and no medical advice. Places from OpenStreetMap (© OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL); all persons and story places are synthetic."
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 1
    value: "### Tables and records\n\nThe demo schema DOAG2026, grouped by the building blocks of the converged database, alphabetical within each group, with the number of rows after loading (run of 10.11.2026):\n\n**JSON**\n\n1. `DIAGNOSES` – 1,326 – diagnoses for the symptom reports\n2. `MEDICATION_RECOMMENDATIONS` – 1,331 – recommended medication per diagnosis\n3. `STG_JSON_DOCS` – 16,550 – all JSON documents as loaded: 1,000 FHIR bundles, Jonas’ app report, map data\n\n**Spatial streaming**\n\n4. `CAR_STREAM` – 267 – stream of the friend’s car, one point every 10 s\n5. `WATCH_STREAM` – 2,051 – Jonas’ watch, one point every 5 s\n\n**Oracle Text, AI Vector Search, Hybrid Vector Index**\n\n6. `CASE_NOTES` – 290 – case library with confirmed diagnoses\n7. `SYMPTOM_REPORTS` – 1,459 – 1,458 symptom reports from the FHIR bundles and Jonas’ app report\n\n**RDF Knowledge Graph – RDF graphs, in triples**\n\n8. `FMA` – 612,982 – Foundational Model of Anatomy, the reference ontology\n9. `KNEE_KG` – 353 – knee knowledge graph: anatomy, findings, injury patterns, Jonas’ report\n\n**SQL Property Graph – tables of the graph `CARE_NETWORK`**\n\n10. `APPOINTMENT_SLOTS` – 435 – appointments per practice and device, free or booked\n11. `DEVICES` – 10 – MRI and X-ray devices per practice\n12. `PATIENTS` – 25 – persons in the care network (P0001 = Jonas)\n13. `PATIENT_PROVIDER_RELATIONS` – 27 – GP and treatment relations\n14. `PROVIDERS` – 28 – practices, radiology centres, hospitals, physiotherapy\n15. `PROVIDER_RELATIONS` – 23 – referrals and cooperations between practices\n\n**Spatial – places of the story**\n\n16. `PARKING_LOTS` – 5 – car parks of the story, with car access\n17. `POIS` – 3 – places of the story: shelter, viewpoint, junction\n18. `ROAD_LINKS` – 28 – simplified road network, links (routing fallback)\n19. `ROAD_NODES` – 22 – simplified road network, nodes (routing fallback)\n20. `TRAIL_SEGMENTS` – 18 – segments of the loop trail with grade\n21. `ZONES` – 5 – dead zone and geofences of the car parks\n\n**Spatial – OpenStreetMap (ODbL)**\n\n22. `OSM_BOUNDARIES` – 2 – city boundaries of Nuremberg and Fürth (OSM)\n23. `OSM_HOSPITALS` – 37 – hospitals (OSM)\n24. `OSM_LAYERS` – 6 – origin and attribution of the OSM extracts\n25. `OSM_PARKING` – 50 – car parks around Pottenstein (OSM)\n26. `OSM_POIS` – 84 – shelters, viewpoints, signposts (OSM)\n27. `OSM_ROADS` – 14,078 – roads between Nuremberg and Bayreuth (OSM)\n28. `OSM_TRAILS` – 1,257 – paths and hiking routes around Pottenstein (OSM)"
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 1
    value: '### Session settings'
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: ALTER SESSION SET TIME_ZONE = 'Europe/Berlin';
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "SET SQLFORMAT ansiconsole\nSET PAGESIZE 1000\nSET LINESIZE 250\nSET LONG 1000000\nSET LONGCHUNKSIZE 250"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: '## Step 1 – What do we know about Jonas? (JSON)'
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 1
    value: "### Jonas’ health record as rows (`JSON_TABLE`)\n\n**Analyzed:** Jonas’ FHIR health record – one of the 1,000 bundles stored as JSON in `stg_json_docs`. `JSON_TABLE` turns every resource of the bundle into one row.\n\n**Expected result:** the patient Jonas, two conditions – the sprain of his right knee in 2021 (*Distorsion rechtes Knie*, resolved) and hay fever –, four observations including his sports profile (hikes two to three times a week) and one medication. A twisted knee looks familiar to him – which is why “just a sprain?” is the tempting answer.\n\n*Slide 15 · notebook 11a, section 4*"
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: "SELECT jt.resource_type,\n       jt.resource_id,\n       COALESCE(jt.code_text, jt.medication)                            AS description,\n       jt.clinical_status,\n       COALESCE(jt.onset, jt.effective)                                 AS since,\n       COALESCE(jt.value_string, jt.value_number || ' ' || jt.value_unit) AS value\nFROM   stg_json_docs s,\n       JSON_TABLE(s.json_document, '$.entry[*].resource'\n         COLUMNS (resource_type    VARCHAR2(30)  PATH '$.resourceType',\n                  resource_id      VARCHAR2(30)  PATH '$.id',\n                  code_text        VARCHAR2(100) PATH '$.code.text',\n                  clinical_status  VARCHAR2(20)  PATH '$.clinicalStatus.coding[0].code',\n                  onset            VARCHAR2(30)  PATH '$.onsetDateTime',\n                  effective        VARCHAR2(30)  PATH '$.effectiveDateTime',\n                  value_string     VARCHAR2(200) PATH '$.valueString',\n                  value_number     NUMBER        PATH '$.valueQuantity.value',\n                  value_unit       VARCHAR2(20)  PATH '$.valueQuantity.unit',\n                  medication       VARCHAR2(200) PATH '$.medication.concept.text')) jt\nWHERE  s.layer = 'fhir_bundles_all_patients'\nAND    s.json_document.entry[0].\"resource\".id.string() = 'P0001'\nORDER  BY jt.resource_type, jt.resource_id;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: '## Step 2 – What happened on the trail? (Spatial streaming)'
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 1
    value: "### The event pattern in the watch stream (`MATCH_RECOGNIZE`)\n\n**Analyzed:** Jonas’ watch stream, one point every 5 seconds, ordered by event time – including the 135 points from the dead zone that arrived 11 minutes late. `MATCH_RECOGNIZE` looks for the pattern walking → impact → standstill → limping.\n\n**Expected result:** one row: walking from 10:05:00, the fall at 11:03:10 with 4.9 g, 8 minutes of standstill until 11:11:10, then limping from 11:11:15 with about 58 steps per minute.\n\n*Slide 16 · notebook 11b, section 5*"
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: "SELECT patient_id,\n       TO_CHAR(walk_start,     'HH24:MI:SS') AS walk_start,\n       TO_CHAR(fall_ts,        'HH24:MI:SS') AS fall_time,\n       impact_g,\n       TO_CHAR(standstill_end, 'HH24:MI:SS') AS standstill_end,\n       standstill_min,\n       TO_CHAR(limping_start,  'HH24:MI:SS') AS limping_start,\n       limping_cadence\nFROM   watch_stream\nMATCH_RECOGNIZE (\n  PARTITION BY patient_id\n  ORDER BY event_ts\n  MEASURES FIRST(walk.event_ts)        AS walk_start,\n           impact.event_ts             AS fall_ts,\n           impact.acc_peak_g           AS impact_g,\n           LAST(still.event_ts)        AS standstill_end,\n           ROUND((CAST(LAST(still.event_ts) AS DATE) - CAST(impact.event_ts AS DATE)) * 1440, 1)\n                                       AS standstill_min,\n           FIRST(limp.event_ts)        AS limping_start,\n           ROUND(AVG(limp.cadence_spm)) AS limping_cadence\n  ONE ROW PER MATCH\n  AFTER MATCH SKIP PAST LAST ROW\n  PATTERN (walk{12,} impact still{6,} limp{6,})\n  DEFINE walk   AS walk.cadence_spm >= 90,\n           impact AS impact.acc_peak_g >= 3,\n           still  AS still.cadence_spm = 0 AND still.acc_peak_g < 2,\n           limp   AS limp.cadence_spm BETWEEN 30 AND 80\n);"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: "### Where it happened: the fall on the trail segment\n\n**Analyzed:** the position of the fall against the trail segments of the loop (nearest segment and distance to its line).\n\n**Expected result:** segment *Abstieg Felsstufe* (T1-S08), less than a metre from the trail line – about 19 % downhill (−18.9 %), the steepest part of the loop.\n\n*Slide 16 · notebook 11b, section 6*"
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: "WITH fall AS (\n  SELECT patient_id, fall_ts, fall_lon, fall_lat\n  FROM   watch_stream\n  MATCH_RECOGNIZE (\n    PARTITION BY patient_id\n    ORDER BY event_ts\n    MEASURES impact.event_ts AS fall_ts,\n             impact.lon      AS fall_lon,\n             impact.lat      AS fall_lat\n    ONE ROW PER MATCH\n    PATTERN (walk{12,} impact still{6,})\n    DEFINE walk   AS walk.cadence_spm >= 90,\n           impact AS impact.acc_peak_g >= 3,\n           still  AS still.cadence_spm = 0 AND still.acc_peak_g < 2\n  )\n)\nSELECT (SELECT f.patient_id FROM fall f)                     AS patient_id,\n       (SELECT TO_CHAR(f.fall_ts, 'HH24:MI:SS') FROM fall f) AS fall_time,\n       t.segment_id,\n       t.segment_name,\n       t.trail_name,\n       t.grade_pct,\n       t.difficulty,\n       ROUND(SDO_NN_DISTANCE(1), 1)                          AS distance_m\nFROM   trail_segments t\nWHERE  SDO_NN(t.geom,\n              (SELECT SDO_GEOMETRY(2001, 4326, SDO_POINT_TYPE(f.fall_lon, f.fall_lat, NULL), NULL, NULL)\n               FROM   fall f),\n              'sdo_num_res=1 unit=M', 1) = 'TRUE';"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: "## Step 3 – What do similar cases say? (Full-text and vector search)"
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 1
    value: "### Keyword “Plopp” (`CONTAINS`)\n\n**Analyzed:** Jonas’ word “Plopp” against 1,458 symptom reports with known diagnoses, full-text search with `CONTAINS` on the Oracle Text index.\n\n**Expected result:** 12 hits, all with the same score: 7 cruciate ligament ruptures (*Vordere Kreuzbandruptur*), all confirmed by MRI. The other 5 – four sprains and one report without diagnosis – say “Kein Plopp, nichts Auffälliges”. Full text finds words, not negations.\n\n*Slide 17 · notebook 11c, section 3*"
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: "SELECT s.report_id,\n       SCORE(1)            AS score,\n       d.diagnosis_label,\n       d.confirmed_by,\n       s.report_text\nFROM   symptom_reports s\nLEFT   JOIN diagnoses d ON d.report_id = s.report_id\nWHERE  s.source = 'fhir'\nAND    CONTAINS(s.report_text, 'Plopp', 1) > 0\nORDER  BY score DESC, s.report_id;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: "### Meaning: what do the 20 nearest reports vote for? (`VECTOR_DISTANCE`)\n\n**Analyzed:** the 20 reports closest in meaning to Jonas’ report (`VECTOR_DISTANCE` with `COSINE` on the embeddings), their diagnoses and the recommended medication.\n\n**Expected result:** sprain (*Kniedistorsion*) 7, medial ligament strain 5, cruciate ligament rupture 3, meniscus lesion 3, contusion 2. Medication for the front runners: diclofenac gel and ibuprofen 400 mg. A pure similarity app would say: just a sprain – rest and cool.\n\n*Slide 17 · notebook 11c, section 8*"
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: "WITH nearest AS (\n  SELECT s.report_id\n  FROM   symptom_reports s\n  WHERE  s.source = 'fhir'\n  ORDER  BY VECTOR_DISTANCE(s.report_embedding, (SELECT j.report_embedding FROM symptom_reports j WHERE j.report_id = 'SR-2026-11-16-0001'), COSINE)\n  FETCH  FIRST 20 ROWS ONLY\n)\nSELECT d.diagnosis_label,\n       COUNT(DISTINCT n.report_id)                                AS reports,\n       LISTAGG(DISTINCT m.medication_text, '; ' ON OVERFLOW TRUNCATE)\n         WITHIN GROUP (ORDER BY m.medication_text)                AS recommended_medications\nFROM   nearest n\nJOIN   diagnoses d ON d.report_id = n.report_id\nLEFT   JOIN medication_recommendations m ON m.diagnosis_id = d.diagnosis_id\nGROUP  BY d.diagnosis_label\nORDER  BY reports DESC;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: "## Step 4 – Which part of the knee is injured? (RDF knowledge graph)"
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 1
    value: "### Jonas’ findings against the injury patterns (`SEM_MATCH`)\n\n**Analyzed:** Jonas’ findings against the five injury patterns of the knee knowledge graph `KNEE_KG`: strong indicators found and needed, counter-indicators, matching mechanism.\n\n**Expected result:** ACL rupture pattern: 3 of 3 strong indicators (pop, rapid swelling, giving way; 2 needed), nothing against it – **fits**. Sprain pattern: 1 of the 2 indicators it needs and 3 counter-indicators – **does not fit**. MCL strain, meniscus lesion and contusion find none of their strong indicators.\n\n*Slide 18 · notebook 11e, section 3*"
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: "SELECT pattern_label,\n       TO_NUMBER(strong_found)   AS strong_found,\n       TO_NUMBER(strong_needed)  AS strong_needed,\n       TO_NUMBER(counter_found)  AS counter_found,\n       TO_NUMBER(mechanism_ok)   AS mechanism_matches,\n       CASE WHEN TO_NUMBER(strong_found) >= TO_NUMBER(strong_needed)\n             AND TO_NUMBER(counter_found) = 0\n             AND TO_NUMBER(mechanism_ok)  > 0\n            THEN 'fits' ELSE 'does not fit' END AS verdict\nFROM   TABLE(SEM_MATCH(\n         'PREFIX kg:   <https://doag2026.example/knee#>\n          PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>\n          PREFIX skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>\n          SELECT ?pattern_label ?strong_needed\n                 (COUNT(DISTINCT ?strong)  AS ?strong_found)\n                 (COUNT(DISTINCT ?counter) AS ?counter_found)\n                 (COUNT(DISTINCT ?mech)    AS ?mechanism_ok)\n          WHERE {\n            ?pattern a kg:InjuryPattern ;\n                     kg:minStrongIndicators ?strong_needed ;\n                     rdfs:label ?pattern_label .\n            FILTER (lang(?pattern_label) = \"de\")\n            OPTIONAL { <https://doag2026.example/knee#Report_SR-2026-11-16-0001> kg:reportsFinding ?strong .\n                       ?pattern kg:hasStrongIndicator ?strong }\n            OPTIONAL { <https://doag2026.example/knee#Report_SR-2026-11-16-0001> kg:reportsFinding ?counter .\n                       ?pattern kg:argumentAgainst ?counter }\n            OPTIONAL { <https://doag2026.example/knee#Report_SR-2026-11-16-0001> kg:reportsMechanism ?mech .\n                       ?pattern kg:requiresMechanism ?mech }\n          }\n          GROUP BY ?pattern_label ?strong_needed',\n         SEM_MODELS('KNEE_KG'), NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, ' ', NULL, NULL,\n         'DOAG2026', 'RDF_NETWORK'))\nORDER  BY TO_NUMBER(strong_found) DESC, TO_NUMBER(counter_found), pattern_label;\n"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: "### From the inferred pattern to diagnosis, next step and medication\n\n**Analyzed:** the conclusions of the rules (inferred triples on `KNEE_FMA_VM`) decide which pattern survives; the knowledge graph and the FMA add diagnosis, structure and next step, the case data the medication of earlier cases with that diagnosis – the bottom row of slide 13 as one query.\n\n**Expected result:** 7 rows. *passt*: ACL tear pattern → *Vordere Kreuzbandruptur* → FMA:44614 *Anterior cruciate ligament*, part of the *Knee joint* → *MRT innerhalb von 48 h*; in 80 earlier ACL ruptures ibuprofen 600 mg (76), enoxaparin 40 mg (45), pantoprazole 20 mg (25). *ausgeschlossen: Gegenindiz*: sprain → ibuprofen 400 mg (76 of 115), diclofenac gel (75). *ausgeschlossen: kein Indiz*: meniscus lesion → ibuprofen 400 mg (36 of 61), diclofenac gel (26).\n\n*Slide 18 · notebook 11e, section 14*"
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: "WITH kg AS (\n  SELECT CASE WHEN ctr IS NOT NULL THEN 'ausgeschlossen: Gegenindiz'\n              WHEN ind IS NULL     THEN 'ausgeschlossen: kein Indiz'\n              ELSE 'passt' END                                           AS verdict,\n         pattern_label,\n         injury_label,\n         diagnosis_code,\n         fma_id || ' ' || fma_label\n           || NVL2(whole_label, ' · Teil von ' || whole_label, '')       AS fma_structure,\n         procedure_label || ' innerhalb von ' || hours || ' h'           AS next_step\n  FROM   TABLE(SEM_MATCH(\n           'PREFIX kg:       <https://doag2026.example/knee#>\n            PREFIX owl:      <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>\n            PREFIX rdfs:     <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>\n            PREFIX skos:     <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>\n            PREFIX oboInOwl: <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#>\n            SELECT ?pattern_label ?ind ?ctr ?diagnosis_code ?injury_label\n                   ?fma_id ?fma_label ?whole_label ?procedure_label ?hours\n            WHERE {\n              <https://doag2026.example/knee#Report_SR-2026-11-16-0001> kg:matchesMechanismOf ?pattern .\n              OPTIONAL { <https://doag2026.example/knee#Report_SR-2026-11-16-0001> ?ind ?pattern .\n                         FILTER (?ind = kg:showsIndicatorOf) }\n              OPTIONAL { <https://doag2026.example/knee#Report_SR-2026-11-16-0001> ?ctr ?pattern .\n                         FILTER (?ctr = kg:showsCounterIndicatorOf) }\n              ?pattern rdfs:label      ?pattern_label ;\n                       kg:suggests     ?injury ;\n                       kg:recommends   ?procedure ;\n                       kg:urgencyHours ?hours .\n              ?injury  rdfs:label           ?injury_label ;\n                       kg:caseDiagnosisCode ?diagnosis_code ;\n                       kg:affects           ?structure .\n              ?procedure rdfs:label ?procedure_label .\n              FILTER (lang(?pattern_label)   = \"de\")\n              FILTER (lang(?injury_label)    = \"de\")\n              FILTER (lang(?procedure_label) = \"de\")\n              ?structure skos:exactMatch ?fma .\n              ?fma rdfs:label  ?fma_label ;\n                   oboInOwl:id ?fma_id .\n              OPTIONAL { ?fma rdfs:subClassOf ?r .\n                         ?r a owl:Restriction ;\n                            owl:someValuesFrom ?whole .\n                         ?whole rdfs:label ?whole_label }\n            }',\n           SEM_MODELS('KNEE_FMA_VM'), NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, ' ', NULL, NULL,\n           'DOAG2026', 'RDF_NETWORK'))),\ncases AS (\n  SELECT diagnosis_code, COUNT(*) AS diagnoses\n  FROM   diagnoses\n  GROUP  BY diagnosis_code)\nSELECT kg.verdict,\n       kg.pattern_label,\n       kg.injury_label                    AS diagnosis,\n       kg.fma_structure,\n       kg.next_step,\n       m.medication_text                  AS medication,\n       COUNT(DISTINCT d.diagnosis_id)     AS cases_with_medication,\n       c.diagnoses                        AS cases_with_diagnosis\nFROM   kg\nJOIN   cases c                        ON c.diagnosis_code = kg.diagnosis_code\nJOIN   diagnoses d                    ON d.diagnosis_code = kg.diagnosis_code\nJOIN   medication_recommendations m   ON m.diagnosis_id   = d.diagnosis_id\nGROUP  BY kg.verdict, kg.pattern_label, kg.injury_label, kg.fma_structure, kg.next_step,\n          m.medication_text, c.diagnoses\nORDER  BY CASE kg.verdict WHEN 'passt' THEN 0 ELSE 1 END, kg.pattern_label, cases_with_medication DESC;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: "## Step 5 – Who can help, and where? (SQL property graph and spatial)"
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 1
    value: "### Why not the obvious way? (`GRAPH_TABLE`)\n\n**Analyzed:** the referral paths from Jonas’ GP (PR01) to the specialists in the care network and their free consultation slots before the talk.\n\n**Expected result:** the sports medicine practice PR30, which Jonas knows, has its first free slot on Wednesday at 11:00 – after the talk. The orthopaedics PR10 has exactly one free slot before the talk: today, Monday, 14:00.\n\n*Slide 19 · notebook 11f, section 4*"
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: "SELECT g.specialist_id,\n       g.specialist,\n       CASE WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1\n                         FROM   patient_provider_relations r\n                         WHERE  r.patient_id  = 'P0001'\n                         AND    r.provider_id = g.specialist_id\n                         AND    r.relation_type = 'war_in_behandlung')\n            THEN 'yes' ELSE 'no' END                                   AS known_to_jonas,\n       TO_CHAR(MIN(g.slot_start), 'DY DD.MM. HH24:MI',\n               'NLS_DATE_LANGUAGE=GERMAN')                            AS earliest_free_slot,\n       COUNT(CASE WHEN g.slot_start < TIMESTAMP '2026-11-17 12:00:00 Europe/Berlin' THEN 1 END)               AS free_slots_before_talk\nFROM   GRAPH_TABLE (care_network\n         MATCH (p IS patient WHERE p.patient_id = 'P0001')\n               -[r1 IS care_relation     WHERE r1.relation_type = 'hat_hausarzt']->  (gp IS provider)\n               -[r2 IS provider_relation WHERE r2.relation_type = 'ueberweist_an']-> (spec IS provider)\n               -[o  IS offers]-> (s IS slot WHERE s.status = 'frei' AND s.slot_type = 'Sprechstunde')\n         WHERE s.slot_start >= TIMESTAMP '2026-11-16 12:00:00 Europe/Berlin'\n         COLUMNS (spec.provider_id AS specialist_id,\n                  spec.name        AS specialist,\n                  s.slot_start)) g\nGROUP  BY g.specialist_id, g.specialist\nORDER  BY MIN(g.slot_start);"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: "### Path, area and drive time in one query\n\n**Analyzed:** specialist–radiology pairs from the property graph with a free consultation and a free knee MRI before the talk, limited to Nuremberg and Fürth by the OSM city boundaries, with the drive time from the car park Hohe Leite (`SDO_GCDR.ELOC_ROUTE`, routing service).\n\n**Expected result:** one row: *Orthopädie am Stadtpark* today at 14:00 → MRI at *Radiologie Nürnberg Nord* tomorrow at 07:30 – 43 minutes and 64.5 km by car. Practices outside the city boundaries (Erlangen, Forchheim, Bayreuth) drop out.\n\n*Slide 19 · notebook 11f, section 8*"
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: "WITH candidates AS (\n  SELECT g.*\n  FROM   GRAPH_TABLE (care_network\n           MATCH (p IS patient WHERE p.patient_id = 'P0001')\n                 -[r1 IS care_relation     WHERE r1.relation_type = 'hat_hausarzt']->   (gp   IS provider)\n                 -[r2 IS provider_relation WHERE r2.relation_type = 'ueberweist_an']->  (spec IS provider)\n                 -[r3 IS provider_relation WHERE r3.relation_type = 'kooperiert_mit']-> (rad  IS provider),\n                 (spec) -[o1 IS offers]-> (s1 IS slot WHERE s1.status = 'frei' AND s1.slot_type = 'Sprechstunde'),\n                 (rad)  -[o2 IS offers]-> (s2 IS slot WHERE s2.status = 'frei' AND s2.slot_type = 'MRT Knie')\n           WHERE s1.slot_start >= TIMESTAMP '2026-11-16 12:00:00 Europe/Berlin'\n             AND s2.slot_start >  s1.slot_start\n             AND s2.slot_start <  TIMESTAMP '2026-11-17 12:00:00 Europe/Berlin'\n           COLUMNS (spec.provider_id AS specialist_id,\n                    spec.name        AS specialist,\n                    spec.lon         AS specialist_lon,\n                    spec.lat         AS specialist_lat,\n                    s1.slot_start    AS consultation,\n                    rad.provider_id  AS radiology_id,\n                    rad.name         AS radiology,\n                    s2.slot_start    AS mri_slot)) g\n  JOIN   providers sp ON sp.provider_id = g.specialist_id\n  JOIN   providers rp ON rp.provider_id = g.radiology_id\n  WHERE  EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM osm_boundaries b WHERE b.name IN ('Nürnberg', 'Fürth') AND SDO_ANYINTERACT(sp.geom, b.geom) = 'TRUE')\n  AND    EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM osm_boundaries b WHERE b.name IN ('Nürnberg', 'Fürth') AND SDO_ANYINTERACT(rp.geom, b.geom) = 'TRUE')\n),\nfirst_choice AS (\n  SELECT specialist_id, specialist, specialist_lon, specialist_lat,\n         MIN(consultation) AS consultation,\n         MIN(mri_slot) KEEP (DENSE_RANK FIRST ORDER BY consultation, mri_slot) AS mri_slot,\n         MIN(radiology)  KEEP (DENSE_RANK FIRST ORDER BY consultation, mri_slot) AS radiology\n  FROM   candidates\n  GROUP  BY specialist_id, specialist, specialist_lon, specialist_lat\n),\nroutes AS (\n  SELECT /*+ MATERIALIZE */\n         f.*,\n         SDO_GCDR.ELOC_ROUTE('fastest', 'km', 'minute',\n                             (SELECT pk.geom.sdo_point.x FROM parking_lots pk WHERE pk.parking_id = 'PK03'),\n                             (SELECT pk.geom.sdo_point.y FROM parking_lots pk WHERE pk.parking_id = 'PK03'),\n                             f.specialist_lon, f.specialist_lat,\n                             'auto') AS route_json\n  FROM   first_choice f\n)\nSELECT specialist,\n       TO_CHAR(consultation, 'DY DD.MM. HH24:MI', 'NLS_DATE_LANGUAGE=GERMAN')       AS consultation,\n       radiology,\n       TO_CHAR(mri_slot,     'DY DD.MM. HH24:MI', 'NLS_DATE_LANGUAGE=GERMAN')       AS mri,\n       ROUND(JSON_VALUE(route_json, '$.routeResponse.route.time'     RETURNING NUMBER)) AS drive_min,\n       ROUND(JSON_VALUE(route_json, '$.routeResponse.route.distance' RETURNING NUMBER), 1) AS drive_km\nFROM   routes\nORDER  BY consultation, drive_min;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: '## Step 6 – Where is the pick-up? (Spatial)'
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 1
    value: "### The nearest car park a car can reach (`SDO_NN`)\n\n**Analyzed:** the car parks nearest to Jonas’ position (`SDO_NN`), filtered by the attribute `car_access`.\n\n**Expected result:** *Wanderparkplatz Hohe Leite* (PK03), 218 m away – the pick-up point.\n\n*Slide 20 · notebook 11g, section 2*"
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: "SELECT p.parking_id,\n       p.name,\n       p.capacity,\n       ROUND(SDO_NN_DISTANCE(1)) AS distance_m\nFROM   parking_lots p\nWHERE  SDO_NN(p.geom,\n              (SELECT s.geom FROM symptom_reports s WHERE s.report_id = 'SR-2026-11-16-0001'),\n              'sdo_batch_size=10 unit=M', 1) = 'TRUE'\nAND    p.car_access = TRUE\nORDER  BY distance_m\nFETCH  FIRST 1 ROW ONLY;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: "### Pick-up: car and Jonas in the geofence\n\n**Analyzed:** two streams – the friend’s car and Jonas’ watch – against the geofence of each car park (`SDO_ANYINTERACT`); the pick-up is when both are inside.\n\n**Expected result:** the car enters the geofence of *Wanderparkplatz Hohe Leite* at 12:51:30, Jonas limps in at 12:54:20 – pick-up at 12:54:20.\n\n*Slide 20 · notebook 11g, section 3*"
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: "WITH car AS (\n  SELECT z.zone_id,\n         MIN(c.event_ts) AS car_enters\n  FROM   car_stream c\n  JOIN   zones z ON SDO_ANYINTERACT(c.geom, z.geom) = 'TRUE'\n  WHERE  z.zone_type = 'Geofence Parkplatz'\n  GROUP  BY z.zone_id\n),\nwalker AS (\n  SELECT z.zone_id,\n         MIN(w.event_ts) AS jonas_enters\n  FROM   watch_stream w\n  JOIN   zones z ON SDO_ANYINTERACT(w.geom, z.geom) = 'TRUE'\n  WHERE  z.zone_type = 'Geofence Parkplatz'\n  AND    w.event_ts  >= TIMESTAMP '2026-11-16 11:17:10 Europe/Berlin'   -- after the app report\n  GROUP  BY z.zone_id\n)\nSELECT zone_id,\n       z.name                                          AS geofence,\n       TO_CHAR(car_enters,   'HH24:MI:SS')             AS car_enters,\n       TO_CHAR(jonas_enters, 'HH24:MI:SS')             AS jonas_enters,\n       TO_CHAR(GREATEST(car_enters, jonas_enters), 'HH24:MI:SS') AS pick_up\nFROM   car\nJOIN   walker USING (zone_id)\nJOIN   zones z USING (zone_id)\nORDER  BY GREATEST(car_enters, jonas_enters);"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: "## Finale – So, where should Jonas go? (all data types in one SELECT)"
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 1
    value: "### One question, one statement\n\n**Analyzed:** the results of steps 1–6 in one `SELECT`: one `WITH` clause per step – JSON, stream, vector, knowledge graph, property graph, spatial, routing – joined on the patient ID.\n\n**Expected result:** one row: `FALL_AT` 11:03 · Abstieg Felsstufe (−18.9 %) · `VECTOR_SEARCH_SAYS` Kniedistorsion · `KNOWLEDGE_GRAPH_SAYS` Muster vordere Kreuzbandruptur · `RECOMMENDATION` MRT innerhalb von 48 h · `PICK_UP` 12:54, Geofence Wanderparkplatz Hohe Leite · `DRIVE_MIN` 43, and the answer in German: *Wanderung beenden und das Knie ruhigstellen. Orthopädie am Stadtpark Dr. Ostertag heute um 14:00 Uhr, MRT morgen um 07:30 Uhr in der Radiologie Nürnberg Nord (MRT01).*\n\n*Slide 21 · notebook 11h*"
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: "WITH\n-- 1. JSON: Jonas' app report as a document\napp_report AS (\n  SELECT jt.patient_id, jt.report_id, jt.created_ts\n  FROM   stg_json_docs s,\n         JSON_TABLE(s.json_document, '$'\n           COLUMNS (patient_id  VARCHAR2(10) PATH '$.patient_id',\n                    report_id   VARCHAR2(30) PATH '$.report_id',\n                    created_ts  VARCHAR2(30) PATH '$.created_ts')) jt\n  WHERE  s.layer = 'symptom_report_jonas'\n),\n-- 2. Streaming + Spatial: fall event and trail segment\nfall AS (\n  SELECT m.patient_id,\n         m.fall_ts,\n         (SELECT t.segment_name || ' (' || t.grade_pct || ' %)'\n          FROM   trail_segments t\n          WHERE  SDO_NN(t.geom,\n                        SDO_GEOMETRY(2001, 4326, SDO_POINT_TYPE(m.fall_lon, m.fall_lat, NULL), NULL, NULL),\n                        'sdo_num_res=1', 1) = 'TRUE') AS fall_segment\n  FROM   watch_stream\n         MATCH_RECOGNIZE (\n           PARTITION BY patient_id\n           ORDER BY event_ts\n           MEASURES impact.event_ts AS fall_ts,\n                    impact.lon      AS fall_lon,\n                    impact.lat      AS fall_lat\n           ONE ROW PER MATCH\n           PATTERN (walk{12,} impact still{6,})\n           DEFINE walk   AS walk.cadence_spm >= 90,\n                  impact AS impact.acc_peak_g >= 3,\n                  still  AS still.cadence_spm = 0 AND still.acc_peak_g < 2\n         ) m\n),\n-- 3. Vector: what do the 20 most similar reports vote for? (as in 11c, section 8)\nsimilar AS (\n  SELECT (SELECT a.patient_id FROM app_report a) AS patient_id,\n         w.vector_diagnosis\n  FROM   (SELECT MAX(v.diagnosis_label) KEEP (DENSE_RANK FIRST ORDER BY v.votes DESC, v.diagnosis_label) AS vector_diagnosis\n          FROM   (SELECT d.diagnosis_label, COUNT(*) AS votes\n                  FROM   (SELECT s.report_id\n                          FROM   symptom_reports s\n                          WHERE  s.source = 'fhir'\n                          ORDER  BY VECTOR_DISTANCE(s.report_embedding,\n                                                    (SELECT j.report_embedding\n                                                     FROM   symptom_reports j\n                                                     WHERE  j.report_id = (SELECT a.report_id FROM app_report a)),\n                                                    COSINE)\n                          FETCH  FIRST 20 ROWS ONLY) n\n                  JOIN   diagnoses d ON d.report_id = n.report_id\n                  GROUP  BY d.diagnosis_label) v) w\n),\n-- 4. RDF: which injury pattern do the findings meet? (patient ID from the graph)\nknowledge AS (\n  SELECT k.patient_id, k.pattern_label, k.recommendation, TO_NUMBER(k.urgency_hours) AS urgency_hours\n  FROM   TABLE(SEM_MATCH(\n           'PREFIX kg:   <https://doag2026.example/knee#>\n            PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>\n            SELECT ?patient_id ?pattern_label ?recommendation ?urgency_hours\n            WHERE {\n              <https://doag2026.example/knee#Report_SR-2026-11-16-0001> kg:patientId ?patient_id .\n              { SELECT ?pattern (COUNT(DISTINCT ?f) AS ?strong_found)\n                 WHERE { <https://doag2026.example/knee#Report_SR-2026-11-16-0001> kg:reportsFinding ?f .\n                         ?pattern kg:hasStrongIndicator ?f }\n                 GROUP BY ?pattern }\n              ?pattern kg:minStrongIndicators ?strong_needed ;\n                       rdfs:label             ?pattern_label ;\n                       kg:recommends          ?procedure ;\n                       kg:urgencyHours        ?urgency_hours .\n              ?procedure rdfs:label ?recommendation .\n              FILTER (?strong_found >= ?strong_needed)\n              FILTER (lang(?pattern_label)  = \"de\")\n              FILTER (lang(?recommendation) = \"de\")\n              FILTER NOT EXISTS { <https://doag2026.example/knee#Report_SR-2026-11-16-0001> kg:reportsFinding ?counter .\n                                  ?pattern kg:argumentAgainst ?counter }\n            }',\n           SEM_MODELS('KNEE_KG'), NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, ' ', NULL, NULL,\n           'DOAG2026', 'RDF_NETWORK')) k\n  ORDER  BY TO_NUMBER(k.urgency_hours)\n  FETCH  FIRST 1 ROW ONLY\n),\n-- 5. Property graph + Spatial: path to consultation and MRI inside Nuremberg/Fuerth\ncare_path AS (\n  SELECT g.patient_id, g.specialist, g.specialist_lon, g.specialist_lat,\n         g.consultation, g.radiology, g.mri_device, g.mri_slot\n  FROM   GRAPH_TABLE (care_network\n           MATCH (p IS patient WHERE p.patient_id = 'P0001')\n                 -[r1 IS care_relation     WHERE r1.relation_type = 'hat_hausarzt']->   (gp   IS provider)\n                 -[r2 IS provider_relation WHERE r2.relation_type = 'ueberweist_an']->  (spec IS provider)\n                 -[r3 IS provider_relation WHERE r3.relation_type = 'kooperiert_mit']-> (rad  IS provider),\n                 (spec) -[o1 IS offers]-> (s1 IS slot WHERE s1.status = 'frei' AND s1.slot_type = 'Sprechstunde'),\n                 (rad)  -[o2 IS offers]-> (s2 IS slot WHERE s2.status = 'frei' AND s2.slot_type = 'MRT Knie')\n           WHERE s1.slot_start >= TIMESTAMP '2026-11-16 12:00:00 Europe/Berlin'\n             AND s2.slot_start >  s1.slot_start\n             AND s2.slot_start <  TIMESTAMP '2026-11-17 12:00:00 Europe/Berlin'\n           COLUMNS (p.patient_id     AS patient_id,\n                    spec.provider_id AS specialist_id,\n                    spec.name        AS specialist,\n                    spec.lon         AS specialist_lon,\n                    spec.lat         AS specialist_lat,\n                    s1.slot_start    AS consultation,\n                    rad.provider_id  AS radiology_id,\n                    rad.name         AS radiology,\n                    s2.device_id     AS mri_device,\n                    s2.slot_start    AS mri_slot)) g\n  JOIN   providers sp ON sp.provider_id = g.specialist_id\n  JOIN   providers rp ON rp.provider_id = g.radiology_id\n  WHERE  g.patient_id = (SELECT a.patient_id FROM app_report a)\n  AND    EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM osm_boundaries b WHERE b.name IN ('Nürnberg', 'Fürth') AND SDO_ANYINTERACT(sp.geom, b.geom) = 'TRUE')\n  AND    EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM osm_boundaries b WHERE b.name IN ('Nürnberg', 'Fürth') AND SDO_ANYINTERACT(rp.geom, b.geom) = 'TRUE')\n  ORDER  BY g.consultation, g.mri_slot\n  FETCH  FIRST 1 ROW ONLY\n),\n-- 6a. Spatial streaming: pick-up = the later geofence entry of car and watch\npick_up AS (\n  SELECT (SELECT a.patient_id FROM app_report a)        AS patient_id,\n         z.name                                         AS car_park,\n         GREATEST((SELECT MIN(c.event_ts) FROM car_stream c\n                   WHERE  SDO_ANYINTERACT(c.geom, z.geom) = 'TRUE'),\n                  (SELECT MIN(w.event_ts) FROM watch_stream w\n                   WHERE  SDO_ANYINTERACT(w.geom, z.geom) = 'TRUE'\n                   AND    w.event_ts >= TIMESTAMP '2026-11-16 11:17:10 Europe/Berlin')) AS pick_up_ts\n  FROM   zones z\n  WHERE  z.zone_id = 'G-PK03'\n),\n-- 6b. Routing: drive time from the car park to the specialist\nroute AS (\n  SELECT /*+ MATERIALIZE */\n         c.patient_id,\n         SDO_GCDR.ELOC_ROUTE('fastest', 'km', 'minute',\n                             (SELECT pk.geom.sdo_point.x FROM parking_lots pk WHERE pk.parking_id = 'PK03'),\n                             (SELECT pk.geom.sdo_point.y FROM parking_lots pk WHERE pk.parking_id = 'PK03'),\n                             c.specialist_lon, c.specialist_lat,\n                             'auto') AS route_json\n  FROM   care_path c\n)\n-- 7. One answer\nSELECT a.patient_id,\n       TO_CHAR(f.fall_ts, 'HH24:MI')                                            AS fall_at,\n       f.fall_segment,\n       sm.vector_diagnosis                                                      AS vector_search_says,\n       kn.pattern_label                                                         AS knowledge_graph_says,\n       kn.recommendation || ' innerhalb von ' || kn.urgency_hours || ' h'      AS recommendation,\n       TO_CHAR(pu.pick_up_ts, 'HH24:MI') || ', ' || pu.car_park                 AS pick_up,\n       ROUND(JSON_VALUE(r.route_json, '$.routeResponse.route.time' RETURNING NUMBER)) AS drive_min,\n       'Wanderung beenden und das Knie ruhigstellen. '\n       || cp.specialist || ' heute um ' || TO_CHAR(cp.consultation, 'HH24:MI') || ' Uhr, '\n       || kn.recommendation || ' morgen um ' || TO_CHAR(cp.mri_slot, 'HH24:MI') || ' Uhr'\n       || ' in der ' || cp.radiology || ' (' || cp.mri_device || ').'            AS answer\nFROM   app_report a\nJOIN   fall      f  ON f.patient_id  = a.patient_id\nJOIN   similar   sm ON sm.patient_id = a.patient_id\nJOIN   knowledge kn ON kn.patient_id = a.patient_id\nJOIN   care_path cp ON cp.patient_id = a.patient_id\nJOIN   pick_up   pu ON pu.patient_id = a.patient_id\nJOIN   route     r  ON r.patient_id  = a.patient_id;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
